rg33 automatic placement of trailing constants and variables

// Regression for the automatically emitted constants and variables blocks
// (05-Sep-26). Three defects, all silent:
//   - the block was stamped with whatever bank happened to be current when the
//     program ended, not the bank it belongs to, so it could land in, and
//     overwrite, another bank
//   - the parser allocated variables before constants but every code generator
//     emitted constants before variables, so the variables were written past
//     the constants instead of where their symbols point
//   - the code generators advanced the bank's cur_pc, so whichever one ran
//     second reported or emitted the block at the wrong address
//
// Both banks leave constants and variables dangling, and the program ends in
// bank 0, so bank 1's trailing block is the one most likely to be misplaced.
// Compared against the stored .ref, which pins bank and address for every word.

100/
       lac [foo:1             // a bank 0 constant holding a bank 1 address
       dac v1
       lac [0d1234
       dac v2
       hlt
bar,   0                      // referenced from bank 1

var v1
var v2

bank 1
200/
foo,   0                      // referenced from bank 0
       lac [bar:0             // a bank 1 constant holding a bank 0 address
       dac w1
       hlt

var w1

bank 0
start 100
